.SH Name
dustbunny - A hobby shell designed for POSIX compatability and Quality-of-Life
.SH License
Dustbunny is licensed under the MIT license. You can view Dustbunnys source code via a GitHub repository at 
.UR https://github.com/dot-underscore1703/dustbunny .UE
.SH Description
Dustbunny is a hobby commandline and scripting shell designed for POSIX compatability and Quality-of-Life.
Dustbunny is currently in early development and not all POSIX features or Quality-of-Life features may be implemented yet.
Please be mindful that, in its current state, Dustbunny should be considered unstable and not yet suitable as a replacement shell.
.SH Usage
dustbunny [OPTIONS]

Options:
     -c, --command <COMMAND>     Execute a command from args rather than interactive input.
     -d, --debug                 Enter debug mode and enable extreme logging (very verbose, will clutter terminal).
     -h, --help                  Print usage
     -t, --tokens                Instead of parsing and executing input, lex into tokens and print the tokens.
     
